{'Figure 1': ('figG1_timeline', 'The rules, 2018–2025, by jurisdiction. Each point is the date a measure took effect (ZTE denial order 15 April 2018, lifted 13 July 2018; Huawei listed 16 May 2019; foreign direct product rule 15 May and 17 August 2020; SMIC listed 18 December 2020; US rules of 7 October 2022, 17 October 2023 and 2 December 2024; YMTC listed 15 December 2022; Japan in force 23 July 2023; Netherlands in force 1 September 2023 and 7 September 2024; AI diffusion rule 13 January 2025, rescinded 13 May 2025; VEU revocation announced 29 August 2025, in force 31 December 2025).'), 'Figure 2': ('fig00_typology', 'One control regime, four responses. Red: the targeted or domestic series; grey dashed: the comparison; navy: Huawei China revenue; pink: the rule that applied. Huawei consumer versus carrier segment revenue (2019 = 100); Huawei overseas versus China revenue; Chinese toolmakers versus the foreign-peer median (log); allied-origin lithography imports (HS 84862039); no domestic immersion scanner was in production use through 2025. Sources: Huawei annual reports; SEC EDGAR, OpenDART, cninfo; GACC.'), 'Figure 3': ('fig02_feed', 'Shielded substitution. (a) Revenue of NAURA, AMEC and ACM Research (2019 = 100, log) against their own 2017–22 log-linear trend and the median of fifteen foreign equipment and equipment-component suppliers (band: interquartile range). (b) Annual revenue growth of the three Chinese firms and the aggregate of the fifteen foreign suppliers. (c) Change in average annual growth, 2023–25 versus 2019–22, by firm; red marks segments covered by the October 2022 rule; Changchuan uses the one comparable post-2022 year and the AMEC pre-period starts in 2020. Sources: audited quarterly and annual accounts in USD.'), 'Figure 4': ('fig04_spec_curve', "Specification curve. (a) 112 estimates of the feed, sorted by size; red against foreign peers, navy against each firm's own pre-2022 trend; dotted lines mark medians. (b) For each estimate, which estimator, counterfactual, data preparation and unit produced it. Quarterly panel 2017Q1–2025Q4, 15 foreign donors; clean re-run of 25 October 2026 (spec_curve_rerun.py in the replication package)."), 'Figure 5': ('fig03_no_ladder', "No clear compliance ladder in bilateral trade. Red: change in log exports 2023–24 versus 2019–21 for the treated destination(s) minus the same change for all other destinations; grey: the same statistic for the 40 largest other destinations (39 with positive flows in the importer-reported source; top row) or 100 random groups of eleven countries (bottom row); 7 of 2,100 placebo values lie beyond the axis range; numbers: Romano–Wolf adjusted one-sided p across the five baskets. Columns: BACI; China's reported exports; importers' reported imports (UN Comtrade). Baskets v2, Appendix A."), 'Figure 6': ('figG2_server_origin', 'United States imports of processing units (HS 847150, the tariff line that carries servers) by origin, USD bn, for 2019, 2022, 2024 and 2025. Other includes Malaysia and Viet Nam. UN Comtrade, United States as reporter, imports by partner.'), 'Figure 7': ('fig05_compliance', "The compliance signature. China share of revenue for toolmakers whose products were listed (red) and two Japanese toolmakers whose main products — dicing saws and general-purpose sputtering — fall largely outside the listed categories (grey). SEC 10-Q revenue by customer location (AMAT, KLA; plotted at quarter end; fiscal fourth quarters, reported only in the 10-K, are not plotted) and EDINET revenue by region (TEL, SCREEN, DISCO, ULVAC; fiscal years ending March, plotted at the fiscal mid-year). Pink: US rules of October 2022 and December 2024; dashed navy: Japan's controls in force July 2023."), 'Appendix Figure A1': ('figA3_estimators', 'Feed estimates by estimator and counterfactual (left) and the gap over foreign peers by year, 2023–25 (right). SDID and ASCM values from the clean re-run of 25 October 2026; year-by-year gaps are means of the quarterly gaps in Appendix Figure A2 (change 2024→2025: aggregate +0.24, rank 2 of 16; NAURA +0.30, rank 2; AMEC +0.42, rank 1; ACM Research +0.10, rank 4).'), 'Appendix Figure A2': ('figA5_feed_dynamics', 'Quarterly revenue gap (log points, seasonally adjusted) of each Chinese toolmaker over its ridge-augmented synthetic control of 15 foreign suppliers, 2022Q4–2025Q4; the three-firm aggregate is the mean of the three log series; band: 5th–95th percentile of the 15 placebo paths (each donor treated in turn, full 2017Q1–2022Q3 pre-period; AMEC is fitted on its own 2019Q1–2022Q3 pre-period); pink: December 2024 designations. End-of-path values are the 2025Q4 gaps.'), 'Appendix Figure A3': ('figA1_hs8_lines', "China's imports of controlled (84862039 other lithography, 84862021 CVD, 84862041 dry etch, 84862029 other deposition) and uncontrolled (84862010 furnaces, 84862022 PVD, 84862031 steppers, 84862050 implanters, 84862049 wet etch/strip) tool lines from the United States, Japan and the Netherlands, indexed to 2019 (log). Other deposition is a small line (0.09 bn dollars in 2019). GACC HS8; 84862090 (mixed) excluded."), 'Appendix Figure A4': ('figA2_permutation', 'Permutation distribution of the compliance-cycle statistic over all 21 assignments of five "controlled" vendors among seven. Statistic: standard deviation of annual changes in China share from 2022 onward (10-K and annual securities reports; AMAT through FY2025, the others through FY2026), averaged within the controlled group minus the uncontrolled group. Firm-level values, pp: Tokyo Electron 12.9, Lam 11.3, SCREEN 11.2, KLA 10.7, Applied Materials 8.6 versus DISCO 4.6 and ULVAC 2.9. Actual assignment +7.2 pp, rank 1 of 21 (p = 0.048); next largest 4.4. Red: the actual assignment.'), 'Appendix Figure A5': ('figA6_lifted', "ZTE's consumer and carrier segment revenue, USD bn at annual average rates, 2015–2025 (left; ZTE annual reports: consumer 35.2 → 15.0 → 33.8 bn yuan and carrier 63.8 → 66.6 → 62.9 bn yuan in 2017, 2019 and 2025) and synthetic difference-in-differences effects against 29 listed peers, pre-period 2015–17, post-period 2019–23, with ranks among 30 placebo paths (right); clean run of 9 October 2026."), 'Appendix Figure A6': ('figA7_origin', "China's dry-etch tool imports (HS 84862041) by origin: shares (left) and values (right), 2019–2026 (2026 January–August). United States–origin share 43.4 → 5.0 percent and Singapore-plus-Malaysia 12.5 → 42.8 percent, 2019 → 2025; Japan peaked at 40.9 percent in 2024. Customs data record the country of origin, not the shipper; the main etch plants in Singapore and Malaysia belong to Applied Materials and Lam Research. GACC."), 'Appendix Figure A7': ('figA4_memory_state', 'The memory makers: revenue 2023–1Q 2026 in CNY bn (prospectus values; 1Q 2026 is the quarter alone), attributable net income of both firms and YMTC weighted return on equity (left); state-linked shareholders from the pre-IPO registers (YMTC filing of 21 August 2026; CXMT prospectus of 27 May 2026) (right). Top four YMTC holders 75.2 percent; CXMT state-owned holders about 54 percent.')}